# Averaging a group of images.
#
# Make a palette row a group first: right-click it, "Make a group", then drop
# more files on that same row. The row shows its shape, e.g. [frame=5].
#
# merge_mean averages every frame into one image, which is what a stack of
# identical exposures wants for noise reduction -- N frames cut the standard
# deviation by sqrt(N).

frames = image("group")

# Raw groups work: image() inserts hot_pixel_repair and a demosaic as usual,
# and the framework runs each of them on EVERY frame. The script says nothing
# about the group -- that is what broadcasting means.
#
# Any single-image algorithm can be applied the same way. This runs on each
# frame, before the merge:
#
#   frames = params(basic_adjust, auto_exposure = 1)(frames)

# over= names the axis to reduce. Optional when the group has one axis, which
# is every group the palette can build today:
#   merged = merge_mean(frames, over="frame")
merged = merge_mean(frames)

display(merged, "merged")
